OL,3,GNEWSAThe woman who has worked for the
OL,4,ANHS since it was founded
OL,5,
OL,6,FA woman who has worked for the NHS
OL,7,Fsince it was formed is still helping
OL,8,Fout in hospitals nearly 80 years later.
OL,10,FAudrey Joughlin, 96, started working
OL,11,Ffor the health service in 1948, and has
OL,12,Fbeen volunteering at the Royal
OL,13,FLiverpool Hospital since 1994.
OL,15,FDuring her career, she diagnosed
OL,16,Fdiseases, but now gives her time
OL,17,Frunning the book trolley service for
OL,18,Fpatients.
